Okay, let me, let me back up a little bit and tell you this.

00:32:45.000 --> 00:32:48.000
God does not want robots in His kingdom.

00:32:49.000 --> 00:32:51.000
We were in God's kingdom.

00:32:51.000 --> 00:32:53.000
And we were members of God's kingdom.

00:32:53.000 --> 00:32:59.000
And we had assignments and we had jobs, work. There was no death.

00:33:00.000 --> 00:33:01.000
Everything was infinite.

00:33:02.000 --> 00:33:08.000
And it was only when God created death after the rebellion in order to bring us into this, this experiment.

00:33:08.000 --> 00:33:10.000
So, God does not want robots.

00:33:10.000 --> 00:33:16.000
In fact, if I ask you if you can make robots that would clean your house, would you do anything you say,

00:33:16.000 --> 00:33:18.000
this is one kind of robots that you can make.

00:33:18.000 --> 00:33:22.000
And another kind of robots that you can make is robots that can think.

00:33:22.000 --> 00:33:28.000
For example, the robot is cleaning the... vacuuming the carpet and your child is going to jump out the window,

00:33:28.000 --> 00:33:31.000
the robot can think and stop and go save the child.

00:33:32.000 --> 00:33:33.000
That's another kind of robot.

00:33:35.000 --> 00:33:38.000
But that kind of robot can tell you "yes" or "no."

00:33:38.000 --> 00:33:42.000
You can say "vacuum the carpet" and the robot will say "no."

00:33:44.000 --> 00:33:47.000
Because he's got this, a mind of his own.

00:33:48.000 --> 00:33:57.000
And there's another kind of robot that has a mind of his own, but appreciates you as the creator of the robot,

00:33:57.000 --> 00:34:03.000
to the point that whatever you tell this robot, he will do, or it will do.

00:34:04.000 --> 00:34:11.000
Not because, because it is designed this way, because that robot is free. It can tell you "no."

00:34:11.000 --> 00:34:13.000
You can say "vacuum the carpet."

00:34:13.000 --> 00:34:15.000
It can say "yes" or "no."

00:34:15.000 --> 00:34:21.000
But it always will obey your order because it appreciates you and knows your greatness.

00:34:21.000 --> 00:34:25.000
It appreciates you greatness and loves you so much that, that it will never say "no."

00:34:25.000 --> 00:34:28.000
Now, what kind of robot would you want in your, your house?

00:34:29.000 --> 00:34:30.000
Dr. Khalifa: Which kind of the three?

